    "title": "Frida Kahlo",
    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Frida Kahlo was a famous Mexican painter. She was born in 1907 in Mexico City, in a blue house that is now a museum. Her father was a photographer, and her mother looked after the home."
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "When Frida was six, she became ill with a disease called polio, and her right leg stayed thin for the rest of her life. At eighteen, she was in a terrible bus accident. She broke many bones and spent months in bed. To help her, her parents put a mirror above her bed and gave her paints."
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Frida began to paint pictures of herself. She said, 'I paint myself because I am alone so often, and because I am the person I know best.' Her paintings are small and colourful, and they often show her pain, her love for Mexico, and animals such as monkeys and birds. She wore traditional Mexican clothes and flowers in her hair."
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "In 1929, Frida married the famous painter Diego Rivera. Their relationship was difficult, but they stayed close friends. Frida died in 1954, aged forty-seven. During her life, she was not as famous as her husband, but today millions of people love her art. Visitors come from all over the world to see her blue house."
      }
    ]
  },
